1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,000
A Mumbai furniture workshop produces 80 kg
of clean plywood offcuts every week.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:12,000
Two kilometres away, a decor business
buys new wood for the same job.

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:18,000
Neither knows the other exists. It has
value — what's missing is coordination.

4
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:24,000
DeadStock Exchange turns one business's surplus
into another's raw material.

5
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Structured listings with real quantities
and dimensions — not a photo and a phone.

6
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:38,000
The workshop lists its surplus
in under a minute.

7
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:48,000
Category, quantity, condition — and the
dimensions that decide if it's usable.

8
00:00:48,000 --> 00:01:05,000
80 kg of clean, untreated plywood offcuts,
15 to 40 cm, available for three days.

9
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:12,000
Now the other side.
The decor business says what it needs.

10
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:25,000
50 kg, nothing under 10 centimetres,
untreated, within 15 kilometres.

11
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:32,000
One compatible match —
and it shows exactly why.

12
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:40,000
Category, quantity, minimum size, condition,
availability window, distance.

13
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:45,000
Six checks, in plain words.
No relevance score, no black box.

14
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:50,000
Two nearby listings didn't match — and it
says which check each one failed.

15
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:57,000
Reserve 50 of the 80. Partial reservation
is the normal case, not an edge case.

16
00:01:57,000 --> 00:02:03,000
The supplier keeps 30.

17
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:10,000
A conditional write in DynamoDB makes
over-reservation impossible.

18
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:18,000
The supplier confirms the material
physically changed hands.

19
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:25,000
Only then is it recorded as reuse — 50 kg,
from a real transaction, not an estimate.

20
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:32,000
React on Amplify, API Gateway to Lambda,
DynamoDB for state.

21
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:38,000
That conditional write is what makes
over-reservation impossible.

22
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:42,000
Here's the row — 30 kg remaining, written
by the reservation you just watched.

23
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:46,000
50 kg redirected from a single match.

24
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:50,000
Four days: our first infra-as-code deploy,
our first DynamoDB transaction,

25
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:53,000
and a matching engine
that explains itself.
